id: pm-graph-fjfn
title: Make source-quality and exact 100/100/100 coverage gates fail closed repo-wide
description: "The current coverage gate measures src only at 81/77/88 and the repository lacks mandatory fail-closed lint, docstring-coverage, and duplication gates. This independently blocks production/publication readiness beyond the compatibility tranche."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[4]: coverage,docstrings,quality,release-blocker
created_at: "2026-08-07T18:45:28.584Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T08:17:46.696Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Every executable authored TypeScript file is enumerated or discovered fail-closed; Coverage is exactly 100/100/100 with behavior-driven tests; Docstring, lint, duplication, and anti-cheat checks are mandatory in release:check and CI"
risk: critical
confidence: high
severity: critical
repro_steps: "Inspect package.json coverageGate and release:check."
expected_result: "All authored runtime source and scripts are governed by exact 100 percent lines, branches, and functions plus strict docstring, lint, and duplication checks that cannot be bypassed by source omission."
actual_result: "coverageGate.sources contains only src with thresholds 81/77/88; no mandatory docstring, lint, or duplication gates are present."
component: quality-gates
customer_impact: "Regressions or undocumented behavior could pass release checks, so the package cannot honestly be called production or publication ready."
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T06:29:09.692Z",codex-agent,"Baseline main be385d3: auditing source discovery, mandatory quality gates and runtime coverage rejection paths. Will add executable failure probes and preserve or raise all existing thresholds; the separate 6zil item records any remaining measured coverage gap."
  "2026-10-16T06:34:42.335Z",codex-agent,"Failure probes exposed two Node runner edge cases: an empty skipped suite has skipped=0 in the aggregate counters; a file with no declared tests counts as one passing file test. Added a dedicated machine-readable completion reporter to require real declared tests per selected file and reject skipped/TODO suite events. Coverage now inventories the repository independently of the configured source list, includes executable scripts and root modules, rejects source omissions and empty patterns, and detects type-only modules by native erasable emit without runtime ignore entries."
  "2026-10-16T06:43:34.999Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: removing only runCoverageGate completion validation produces three assertion failures (empty skipped suite, empty TODO suite, zero-test file); restoring it passes all 15 focused tests. Reverting only its repository inventory to configured-source selection produces one failure for omitted root/script modules. Existing presence rejection of an unloaded module and nonexistent configured path is preserved. Linked pm test --run --progress passes; test-result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so its receipt is recorded here without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-16T06:49:19.638Z",codex-agent,"Refined reporter diagnosis with an isolated coverage probe: Node excludes filenames beginning test- from source coverage even with an explicit include; a reporter named completion-reporter.ts is measured at 11/11 lines, 6/6 branches and 1/1 functions, including when configured directly as a reporter. Renamed the authored file and removed the unnecessary generated-copy workaround. The new 18-test focused suite passes; nested authored directories named dist remain governed, empty files cannot borrow a sibling test, and an unavailable real runtime fails closed."
  "2026-10-16T06:56:35.912Z",codex-agent,"Additional real bypass reproduced: native Node accepts --test-coverage-lines=99.7 but a 99.34-percent fixture exits 0 because fractional CLI floors are truncated. Added independent exact LCOV counter enforcement for all three dimensions, rejecting missing/impossible counters and retaining decimal precision. The end-to-end fractional-floor regression plus counter validations bring the focused suite to 20 passing tests. The earlier complete run passed 340/340 with all ten runtime modules reported at 99.71/94.97/100; final npm and Bun gates are being repeated with exact counter enforcement."
  "2026-10-16T07:04:39.629Z",codex-agent,"Final behavioral proofs: in isolated copies, changing only runCoverageGate to configured-source discovery fails 1/1 omission regression; removing completion validation fails 3/3 skipped/TODO/zero-test regressions; removing exact LCOV enforcement fails 1/1 fractional-floor regression. Restored code passes 20/20 focused tests on Node 22.23.1, 24.19.0 and 26.12.0. Linked pm test --run --progress passes 20/20. Clean-HOME npm release:check passes 342/342 with 10/10 runtime modules present and 99.71/95.04/100 coverage; lint and duplication are clean, all 95 governed declarations documented, audit reports no vulnerabilities. Final Bun gate pending."
  "2026-10-16T07:09:06.444Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: clean-HOME npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass 342/342 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs. All 10 runtime TypeScript modules present; 99.71% lines / 95.04% branches / 100% functions, with exact independent floors 99.7/94.9/100. Changelog regenerated, canonical lint/docstrings/zero-duplication gates pass, production audit clean. Leave all backlog items unclosed for orchestrator review; full-coverage and historical-timeout gaps remain documented."
  "2026-10-16T07:10:12.876Z",codex-agent,"Precision note for the final receipts: npm measures 99.71/95.04/100 and Bun measures 99.71/95.05/100 (lines/branches/functions); both pass 342/342 with all ten runtime modules present. The minimum across the two is 99.71/95.04/100. Claims remain released and no items were closed."
  "2026-10-16T07:35:04.402Z",codex-agent,"CI follow-up verified: deterministic suggestion ranking and both analytics help flags hit src/index.ts:2332 and :1027 under real Node 22 and 26 coverage. Removing only substring-ranking priority makes the new SDK-harness assertion fail; removing only the help-flag parser branch makes the -h positional assertion fail. Correct fixtures pass, including the linked ranking test. Full npm/Node26 and Bun-launcher/Node22 release checks now pass 344/344 each, no failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs; minimum coverage 99.71/95.08/100 over all ten runtime modules. Exact floors unchanged at 99.7/94.9/100."
  "2026-10-16T07:59:48.627Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 (PR #140): confirmed Windows-shaped glob paths are compared directly against slash-normalized completion receipts. Plan: use one comparison-only path key for selected files and event paths, preserve native runner arguments, add Windows/POSIX helper and completion regressions with behavioral revert proof, and exercise coverage-gate tests in the existing Windows CI job. Branch is clean and includes current origin/main; thresholds remain 99.7/94.9/100."
  "2026-10-16T08:01:26.559Z",codex-agent,"Implemented shared testPathKey for declared-event and selected-glob comparisons, including Windows drive/case normalization and POSIX case preservation; runner inputs retain native spelling. Focused suite passes 23/23. Behavioral revert: restore only assertCompleteRun from pre-fix HEAD, retain helper/tests, then run node --test --test-name-pattern='coverage completion accepts Windows-shaped' test/coverage-gate.test.ts: 0 pass / 1 fail, exit 1, with coverage-gate: incomplete test run (no declared tests or missing summary). Restoring the fix passes the regression; missing selected files and synthetic empty-file events still fail closed. Existing Windows CI job now also exercises the real gate/glob/receipt fixture and cross-platform comparison regressions."
  "2026-10-16T08:17:45.402Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 verification complete. Clean-HOME npm run release:check on Node 26.12.0 passes 347/347 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/TODO, coverage 4789/4803 lines (99.7085%), 1127/1186 branches (95.0253%), 237/237 functions. Clean-HOME bun run release:check (Bun 1.3.5, Node 22.23.1) passes 347/347, zero fail/skip/cancel/TODO, coverage 4789/4803 lines (99.7085%), 1126/1185 branches (95.0211%), 237/237 functions. All ten runtime modules reported; unchanged floors 99.7/94.9/100; 96 declarations documented; zero duplication and production audit findings. node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts passes 23/23; Windows CI selection passes 4/4 locally; pm test --run --progress passes both linked commands (result recording remains disabled by existing project policy). Revert base is 86ae0e3: restoring only assertCompleteRun fails the new Windows-shaped receipt regression 0 pass / 1 fail; restored fix passes. pm validate and merge reconcile --dry-run pass with no pending receipts or repairs; clean-HOME strict health with merge drivers passes. Normal-HOME health sees an existing global extension host-version skew; no configuration changes made. Item remains in progress and unclosed; releasing claim before push."
